<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Atlantes of Tula</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900–<a href="/years/1100">1100</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Atlantean figures of Tula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Atlantes of Tula are four colossal basalt columns carved as Toltec warriors, about 4.6 metres tall, standing on top of Pyramid B at the archaeological site of Tula in Hidalgo, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. Carved around 900–1100 CE, they once supported the roof of the temple, and each wears a butterfly-shaped breastplate and carries an atlatl and darts.</p></div>
